.Rproj.user
.Rhistory
.RData
.RDataTmp*
.Ruserdata
# Litter from a headless `Rscript main.R`/`Rscript run_tests.R` run: dev.new() falls back to a
# default pdf() device when no display is available, auto-numbering Rplots1.pdf, Rplots2.pdf, ...
# on repeated calls (see Diagnostics.R's and run_tests.R's own comments on this). Not a real
# output -- has leaked into the working tree and gotten accidentally committed twice already.
Rplots*.pdf
*.csv
!tests/testthat/fixtures/**/*.csv
!israeli_cbs_wfh_2digit.csv

# Checkpoint 9: persisted output layer. Tracked in git (not blanket-ignored). The `*.csv` rule
# above would otherwise still catch every CSV in here, hence the negation. See docs/ROADMAP.md
# Checkpoint 9.
!outputs/**

# LaTeX build artifacts from compiling paper/paper.tex (pdflatex + bibtex four-pass; see the
# compile notes in paper/notes/results_digest.md). Regenerated on every build, so they only create
# diff noise. paper/paper.pdf is deliberately NOT listed here -- the compiled paper is a tracked
# deliverable, same convention as outputs/ above. No blanket *.pdf rule exists in this file
# (Rplots*.pdf above is name-anchored), so the PDF needs no negation to stay tracked.
paper/*.aux
paper/*.bbl
paper/*.log
paper/*.blg
paper/*.out
paper/*.toc
paper/*.fls
paper/*.fdb_latexmk

# Personal Claude Code overrides. Holds the paper-recompile PostToolUse hook, whose command
# hardcodes this machine's MiKTeX location (~/AppData/Local/Programs/MiKTeX/...), so it is not
# portable to a co-author's machine and must not be committed. A shared, portable
# .claude/settings.json is deliberately NOT ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json
